        "description": "Resolves, for every configured member, the newest audit event that deployed the member's current image; when all members share one operation, redeploys each member's recorded prior image — validating every member before the first provider submission and submitting every member before waiting so rollouts overlap — and returns per-member terminal events. Members whose current images were not deployed by one shared operation are rejected with a conflict; revert them individually via the target reverts route. A promotion hold never blocks a revert, and a failed revert is never compensated; the response names members needing manual intervention. Reverting the pair from the production console redeploys the orchestrating back-end itself; the waited result is only guaranteed when driven from the staging console.",
